      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Section 10 is amended to add new subsections.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "New powers are granted."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-act-1988-sec-8-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "restriction",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Restricts certain activities",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Subsection (5) prohibits the formation of companies for specific purposes.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Certain activities are restricted."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-act-1988-sec-9",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9 Section 9",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-amendment-act-1988#sec-9"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-amendment-act-1988.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-amendment-act-1988.pdf, p.6",
      "values:originalText": "Section 10A of the Principal Act is repealed and the following section\nis substituted:\nCommission to notify Minister of significant business activities\n\"10A. (1) If the Commission, or a subsidiary of the Commission,\nproposes:\n(a) to form, or participate in the formation of, a company;\n\nTelecommunications\nAmendment\nNo. 121, 1988\n(b) to enter into a partnership;\n(c) to enter into a joint venture or an arrangement for the sharing of\nprofits;\n(d) to acquire a major shareholding in a company;\n(e) to acquire a substantial business; or\n(f) to undertake a significant new business activity;\nthe Commission shall immediately give written notice of particulars of the\nproposed activity to the Minister.\n\"(2) The Minister may, by written notice given to the Commission,\nmake guidelines to be applied by the Commission in determining whether\nan activity is an activity falling within paragraph (1) (d), (e) or (f).\n\"(3) For the purposes of this section, the question whether a body\ncorporate is a subsidiary of another body corporate shall be determined in\nthe same manner as the question whether a corporation is a subsidiary of\nanother corporation is determined under the Companies Act\n1981.\n\"(4) This section does not limit the operation of subsection 100 (2).\".",
      "skos:definition": "Section 10A of the Principal Act is repealed and the following section\nis substituted:\nCommission to notify Minister of significant business activities\n\"10A. (1) If the Commission, or a subsidiary of the Commission,\nproposes:\n(a) to form, or participate in the formation of, a company;\n\nTelecommunications\nAmendment\nNo. 121, 1988\n(b) to enter into a partnership;\n(c) to enter into a joint venture or an arrangement for the sharing of\nprofits;\n(d) to acquire a major shareholding in a company;\n(e) to acquire a substantial business; or\n(f) to undertake a significant new business activity;\nthe Commission shall immediately give written notice of particulars of the\nproposed activity to the Minister.\n\"(2) The Minister may, by written notice given to the Commission,\nmake guidelines to be applied by the Commission in determining whether\nan activity is an activity falling within paragraph (1) (d), (e) or (f).\n\"(3) For the purposes of this section, the question whether a body\ncorporate is a subsidiary of another body corporate shall be determined in\nthe same manner as the question whether a corporation is a subsidiary of\nanother corporation is determined under the Companies Act\n1981.\n\"(4) This section does not limit the operation of subsection 100 (2).\".",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-act-1988-sec-9-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d75d8e6ceadcf42e19764a1946ed0d9dc386970bcd6a86dbbd4e45b70779d743",
      "skos:note": "Repeals Section 10A and substitutes a new section."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-amendment-act-1988#sec-9",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9 Section 9",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 6,
      "values:originalText": "Section 10A of the Principal Act is repealed and the following section\nis substituted:\nCommission to notify Minister of significant business activities\n\"10A. (1) If the Commission, or a subsidiary of the Commission,\nproposes:\n(a) to form, or participate in the formation of, a company;\n\nTelecommunications\nAmendment\nNo. 121, 1988\n(b) to enter into a partnership;\n(c) to enter into a joint venture or an arrangement for the sharing of\nprofits;\n(d) to acquire a major shareholding in a company;\n(e) to acquire a substantial business; or\n(f) to undertake a significant new business activity;\nthe Commission shall immediately give written notice of particulars of the\nproposed activity to the Minister.\n\"(2) The Minister may, by written notice given to the Commission,\nmake guidelines to be applied by the Commission in determining whether\nan activity is an activity falling within paragraph (1) (d), (e) or (f).\n\"(3) For the purposes of this section, the question whether a body\ncorporate is a subsidiary of another body corporate shall be determined in\nthe same manner as the question whether a corporation is a subsidiary of\nanother corporation is determined under the Companies Act\n1981.\n\"(4) This section does not limit the operation of subsection 100 (2).\"."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-act-1988-sec-9-norm",
