      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-amendment-act-1988.pdf, p.15",
      "values:originalText": "Section 75 of the Principal Act is amended by omitting subsection\n(2) and substituting the following subsection:\n\"(2) Money of the Commission not immediately required for the purposes\nof the Commission may be invested in any manner that is consistent with\nsound commercial practice.\".\n\nTelecommunications\nAmendment\nNo. 121, 1988\nRepeal of sections 79 and 79A",
      "skos:definition": "Section 75 of the Principal Act is amended by omitting subsection\n(2) and substituting the following subsection:\n\"(2) Money of the Commission not immediately required for the purposes\nof the Commission may be invested in any manner that is consistent with\nsound commercial practice.\".\n\nTelecommunications\nAmendment\nNo. 121, 1988\nRepeal of sections 79 and 79A",
      "cml:asserts": [
