    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-act-1988-sec-22",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "22 After section 110 of the Principal Act the following sections are",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-amendment-act-1988#sec-22"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-amendment-act-1988.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-amendment-act-1988.pdf, p.16",
      "values:originalText": "inserted:\nPublic Works Committee Act\n\"110A. The Public\nWorks\nCommittee\nAct\n1969 does not apply in\nrelation to the Commission.\nLands Acquisition Act\n\"110B. ( 1 ) The Lands Acquisition\nAct 1955 does not apply in relation\nto the acquisition of land, or an interest in land, by the Commission by\nagreement.\n\nTelecommunications\nAmendment\nNo. 121, 1988\n\"(2) In subsection (1):\n'interest', in relation to land, means:\n(a) a legal or equitable estate or interest in the land; or\n(b) a right, power or privilege over, or in relation to, the land.\".\nConsequential and minor amendments of Principal Act",
      "skos:definition": "inserted:\nPublic Works Committee Act\n\"110A. The Public\nWorks\nCommittee\nAct\n1969 does not apply in\nrelation to the Commission.\nLands Acquisition Act\n\"110B. ( 1 ) The Lands Acquisition\nAct 1955 does not apply in relation\nto the acquisition of land, or an interest in land, by the Commission by\nagreement.\n\nTelecommunications\nAmendment\nNo. 121, 1988\n\"(2) In subsection (1):\n'interest', in relation to land, means:\n(a) a legal or equitable estate or interest in the land; or\n(b) a right, power or privilege over, or in relation to, the land.\".\nConsequential and minor amendments of Principal Act",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-act-1988-sec-22-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4a9e3a87651ae441b3c54d84d60c61b5280cf2a659e40f0611151ad82f1639b7",
      "skos:note": "Inserts sections from other acts"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-amendment-act-1988#sec-22",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "22 After section 110 of the Principal Act the following sections are",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 16,
      "values:originalText": "inserted:\nPublic Works Committee Act\n\"110A. The Public\nWorks\nCommittee\nAct\n1969 does not apply in\nrelation to the Commission.\nLands Acquisition Act\n\"110B. ( 1 ) The Lands Acquisition\nAct 1955 does not apply in relation\nto the acquisition of land, or an interest in land, by the Commission by\nagreement.\n\nTelecommunications\nAmendment\nNo. 121, 1988\n\"(2) In subsection (1):\n'interest', in relation to land, means:\n(a) a legal or equitable estate or interest in the land; or\n(b) a right, power or privilege over, or in relation to, the land.\".\nConsequential and minor amendments of Principal Act"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-act-1988-sec-22-norm",
