    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-act-1988-sec-29",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "29 Section 29",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-amendment-act-1988#sec-29"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-amendment-act-1988.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-amendment-act-1988.pdf, p.18",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A delegation given under section 33 of the Principal Act (other\nthan a delegation of the Commission's powers under subsection 11 (2) of\nthe Principal Act) and in force immediately before the commencement of\nsection 12 of this Act has effect, after that commencement, as if it were a\ndelegation given under section 10B of the Principal Act as amended by this\nAct.\n(2) A delegation given under section 33 of the Principal Act (being a\ndelegation of the Commission's powers under subsection 11 (2) of the\nPrincipal Act) and in force immediately before the commencement of\nsection 12 of this Act has effect, after that commencement, as if it were a\ndelegation given under subsection 27 (1) of the Principal Act as amended\nby this Act.\n(3) If section 12 of this Act commences before section 14 of this Act,\nsection 10B and paragraph 27 (1) (b) of the Principal Act as amended by\nthis Act have effect, after the commencement of section 12 of this Act and\nuntil the commencement of section 14 of this Act, as if a reference to an\nemployee were a reference to an officer or employee of the Corporation.\nExisting Managing Director",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A delegation given under section 33 of the Principal Act (other\nthan a delegation of the Commission's powers under subsection 11 (2) of\nthe Principal Act) and in force immediately before the commencement of\nsection 12 of this Act has effect, after that commencement, as if it were a\ndelegation given under section 10B of the Principal Act as amended by this\nAct.\n(2) A delegation given under section 33 of the Principal Act (being a\ndelegation of the Commission's powers under subsection 11 (2) of the\nPrincipal Act) and in force immediately before the commencement of\nsection 12 of this Act has effect, after that commencement, as if it were a\ndelegation given under subsection 27 (1) of the Principal Act as amended\nby this Act.\n(3) If section 12 of this Act commences before section 14 of this Act,\nsection 10B and paragraph 27 (1) (b) of the Principal Act as amended by\nthis Act have effect, after the commencement of section 12 of this Act and\nuntil the commencement of section 14 of this Act, as if a reference to an\nemployee were a reference to an officer or employee of the Corporation.\nExisting Managing Director",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-act-1988-sec-29-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-act-1988-sec-29-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-act-1988-sec-29-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "53f8b02a57eb95c8b5899d5657f9fe7187d1f067762c4d339f1deda935808fc0"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-amendment-act-1988#sec-29",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "29 Section 29",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 18,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A delegation given under section 33 of the Principal Act (other\nthan a delegation of the Commission's powers under subsection 11 (2) of\nthe Principal Act) and in force immediately before the commencement of\nsection 12 of this Act has effect, after that commencement, as if it were a\ndelegation given under section 10B of the Principal Act as amended by this\nAct.\n(2) A delegation given under section 33 of the Principal Act (being a\ndelegation of the Commission's powers under subsection 11 (2) of the\nPrincipal Act) and in force immediately before the commencement of\nsection 12 of this Act has effect, after that commencement, as if it were a\ndelegation given under subsection 27 (1) of the Principal Act as amended\nby this Act.\n(3) If section 12 of this Act commences before section 14 of this Act,\nsection 10B and paragraph 27 (1) (b) of the Principal Act as amended by\nthis Act have effect, after the commencement of section 12 of this Act and\nuntil the commencement of section 14 of this Act, as if a reference to an\nemployee were a reference to an officer or employee of the Corporation.\nExisting Managing Director"
    },
