    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-act-1988-sec-30",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "30 Section 30",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-amendment-act-1988#sec-30"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-amendment-act-1988.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-amendment-act-1988.pdf, p.18",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The person who, immediately before the commencement of\nsection 12 of this Act, holds office as Managing Director continues to hold\nthat office.\n(2) Subsections 22 (2) and (5) and 23 (1), sections 24, 26 and 27 and\nsubsections 28 (1) and (2) of the Principal Act, and the By-laws made for\nthe purposes of subsection 22 (5) of the Principal Act (being the By-laws in\nforce immediately before the commencement of section 12 of this Act),\ncontinue to apply in relation to the person, and so apply as if references to\na Commissioner were references to the Managing Director and as if the\nreference in paragraph 28 (2) (b) of the Principal Act to subsection (3)\nwere a reference to section 26 of the Principal Act as amended by this Act.\n(3) Sections 33H to 33L (inclusive) of the Principal Act as amended by\nthis Act do not apply in relation to the person.\n(4) Subsections (2) and (3) cease to have effect if the person is appointed\nas Managing Director after the commencement of section 12 of this Act\n\nTelecommunications\nAmendment\nNo. 121, 1988\n(whether at the end of the present period of appointment of the person or\notherwise).\nExisting Chief General Manager",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The person who, immediately before the commencement of\nsection 12 of this Act, holds office as Managing Director continues to hold\nthat office.\n(2) Subsections 22 (2) and (5) and 23 (1), sections 24, 26 and 27 and\nsubsections 28 (1) and (2) of the Principal Act, and the By-laws made for\nthe purposes of subsection 22 (5) of the Principal Act (being the By-laws in\nforce immediately before the commencement of section 12 of this Act),\ncontinue to apply in relation to the person, and so apply as if references to\na Commissioner were references to the Managing Director and as if the\nreference in paragraph 28 (2) (b) of the Principal Act to subsection (3)\nwere a reference to section 26 of the Principal Act as amended by this Act.\n(3) Sections 33H to 33L (inclusive) of the Principal Act as amended by\nthis Act do not apply in relation to the person.\n(4) Subsections (2) and (3) cease to have effect if the person is appointed\nas Managing Director after the commencement of section 12 of this Act\n\nTelecommunications\nAmendment\nNo. 121, 1988\n(whether at the end of the present period of appointment of the person or\notherwise).\nExisting Chief General Manager",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-act-1988-sec-30-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-act-1988-sec-30-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-act-1988-sec-30-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-act-1988-sec-30-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "139fb86c61cb3e6ec50a0d9dbd548d83a87253ddfbd9ce349c9fe6f7cd7f8b31"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-amendment-act-1988#sec-30",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "30 Section 30",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 18,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The person who, immediately before the commencement of\nsection 12 of this Act, holds office as Managing Director continues to hold\nthat office.\n(2) Subsections 22 (2) and (5) and 23 (1), sections 24, 26 and 27 and\nsubsections 28 (1) and (2) of the Principal Act, and the By-laws made for\nthe purposes of subsection 22 (5) of the Principal Act (being the By-laws in\nforce immediately before the commencement of section 12 of this Act),\ncontinue to apply in relation to the person, and so apply as if references to\na Commissioner were references to the Managing Director and as if the\nreference in paragraph 28 (2) (b) of the Principal Act to subsection (3)\nwere a reference to section 26 of the Principal Act as amended by this Act.\n(3) Sections 33H to 33L (inclusive) of the Principal Act as amended by\nthis Act do not apply in relation to the person.\n(4) Subsections (2) and (3) cease to have effect if the person is appointed\nas Managing Director after the commencement of section 12 of this Act\n\nTelecommunications\nAmendment\nNo. 121, 1988\n(whether at the end of the present period of appointment of the person or\notherwise).\nExisting Chief General Manager"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-act-1988-sec-30-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "30(1) Section 30",
